<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Arsames I</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Arsames I was a king of Sophene, and possibly of Commagene, in the 3rd century BCE, a member of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orontid-dynasty">Orontid dynasty</a> that had ruled <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armenia">Armenia</a> under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/achaemenid-empire">Achaemenids</a>. He is credited with founding the cities of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arsamosata">Arsamosata</a> and Arsameia, and he is said to have sheltered the Seleucid prince Antiochus Hierax during the dynastic wars of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seleucid-empire">Seleucid Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/arsames-i.jpg" alt="Arsames I" width="320" height="165" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rs4815 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arsames_I_coin_240_BC.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
